Chapter 1: The Nature of Hypertext and Primedia

"By 'hypertext' I mean non-sequential writing--text that branches and allows choices to the reader, best read at an interactive screen."

Section 1.1: The Docuverse Continuum
The world of ideas is not a set of isolated pigeonholes, but a universal continuum. EVERYTHING IS DEEPLY INTERTWINGLED. In an important sense there are no 'subjects' at all; there is only all knowledge, since the brute facts, but the aspects of reality and the thoughts which have already been thought are interconnectable into the same great tangle.

Section 1.2: Intrinsic Bidirectionality
Links must be two-way and visible. A link to any portion is present on all manifestations. Traditional one-way links sever connections and decay into dead ends. In the Xanadu architecture, butterfly links bind content addresses across hypertime.

Section 1.3: Transclusion and Provenance
Transclusion is not copy-and-paste. Quotation must preserve identity: when text is quoted into a new context, it remains the exact same bytes in the author's permascroll.
homed.dimsd.editionsd.edition-ofcurrentCommentary on Xanadulogical Systems and Multi-Rank Manifolds

Section A: On the Interconnected Fabric of Knowledge
The fundamental axiom of Xanadu is that 
Section B: Dialectic Critique of Web Hierarchies
Conventional hierarchical filesystems and one-way web links force artificial hierarchies onto fluid knowledge networks. Xanadu replaces static URLs with content-addressed primedia coordinates and sovereign permascrolls.

Section C: The Eightfold Relational Taxonomy
Links connect ideas through eight distinct semantic modes: commentary, illustration, disagreement, authorship, quotation, associative context, formatting presentation, and multi-dimensional zigzag manifolds.
